<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23658" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-ordĭnātus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>not arranged</i>, <i>disordered</i>, <i>irregular</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inordinati et incompositi milites,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					22, 50, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hostes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					35, 29, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inordinati in proelium ruunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					23, 27, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ordo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. p. 292</span></i>
			 Oud. — <i>Sup.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inordinatissimi pili,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					22, 22, 45, § 91</span></i>
			.—In <i>neutr. absol.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">idque ex inordinato in ordinem adduxit,</span>”
				<i>disorder</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Univ. 3, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 10, 46</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 2, 23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 4,
				1</span></i>.—<i>Adv.</i> in two forms.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnordĭnātē</span></b> ,
				<i>irregularly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">febres redire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 3,
					3</span></i>
			; so 1, 4. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnordĭnātim</span></b> , <i>irregularly</i>:  acies non
			inordinatim incedebant, <i><span class="en">Amm. 19, 7,
		3</span></i>.</div>
